                <pb facs="0688" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg606"/>

                <head>[Enclosure No. 3.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Maximilian’s answer.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Marquis</hi>: It is with sincere
                    satisfaction that I receive from your hands the letters of credence by which his
                    Majesty the Emperor of the French has accredited you near my person.</p>
                <p>I am happy to see in you the representative of a sovereign who has done so much
                    for the future of Mexico, and towards whom, as you have remarked, this country
                    manifests sentiments of the most sincere gratitude.</p>
                <p>I do not hesitate to believe that the bonds of friendship and the fraternal
                    relations which unite France to Mexico will find in you a faithful interpreter;
                    and, on my part, I will see with pleasure these ties drawn closer and closer
                    between the two empires and the two peoples.</p>
            </div>
